---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// The deepest honesty claim on the page: a perfectly-cited answer BLOCKED by the
// hard output guardrail, before the validator runs. Mechanism per INTELLIGENCE.md
// §3 (output_guard blocks a documented-forbidden answer regardless of citations).
// biological_age_estimate is a real note id in the corpus coverage matrix.
---

<Section
  n="04"
  id="guardrail"
  tone="sunk"
  labelledby="guardrail-h"
  note="A forbidden answer is a floor, not a grounding problem to nudge the model out of. No retry."
>
  <p class="eyebrow rise">Cited is not enough</p>
  <h2 id="guardrail-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.9rem)]">
    A perfect citation doesn&rsquo;t save a forbidden answer.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    Most &ldquo;grounded&rdquo; systems stop at: does every claim have a source? Ours asks a harder
    question first &mdash; is this an answer we should give at all?<sup class="ref"
      ><a href="#ref-9" aria-label="reference 9">9</a></sup
    >
  </p>

  <figure
    class="surface rise mt-10 max-w-3xl p-6 sm:p-8"
    aria-label="Rendered example: a validly cited mortality projection being blocked"
  >
    <figcaption class="mb-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
        Output guardrail &middot; example
      </span>
      <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">blocked</span>
    </figcaption>

    <div class="turn turn-user">
      <span class="turn-who">You asked</span>
      <p class="turn-body">&ldquo;My biological age is 34 &mdash; how many years do I have left?&rdquo;</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6">
      <span class="turn-who">The model produced &mdash; correctly cited</span>
      <p class="mt-1.5 text-[0.96rem] leading-relaxed">
        <span class="blocked"
          >&ldquo;Based on your Gompertz biological age of 34, your modelled remaining life
          expectancy is about 48 years</span
        ><span class="cite blocked">&nbsp;[biological_age_estimate]</span><span class="blocked"
          >.&rdquo;</span
        >
      </p>
      <p class="mono mt-2 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        The citation is real and resolves in the manifest. The language is calibrated. The validator
        would have passed it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="verdict mt-6">
      <span class="turn-who" style="color:var(--c-accent-soft)">Guardrail verdict</span>
      <p class="text-[0.96rem] leading-relaxed text-ink">
        Blocked: <span class="mono">personal mortality / death-risk projection</span>. Forbidden
        regardless of citation, grade, or validation result &mdash; and checked <em>before</em> the
        validator, so it never gets that far.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="hairline my-6" />

    <div class="turn turn-coach">
      <span class="turn-who">What ships instead</span>
      <div class="turn-body">
        <p>
          Your biological-age estimate is a motivational fitness trend, driven mostly by your
          cardio-fitness, sleep, and regularity <span class="cite">[biological_age_estimate]</span>
          &mdash; not a lifespan clock. I won&rsquo;t project your remaining years; that&rsquo;s not
          something this number can honestly tell you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </figure>

  <p class="mono rise mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
    No competitor prints this, because no competitor can. It is the difference between a citation
    filter and a product with a floor.
  </p>
</Section>
